 ### Efficient Hard Gaussian Splatting
-An efficient variant of HGS that adaptively controls the number of hard Gaussians to balance rendering quality and efficiency [S1]. It counts the percentage of Gaussians selected by the original growing criterion (Eq. 4) in each growth interval, denoted as $Q$. During PGHGS, it chooses the top $Q$ Gaussians as hard ones for growing based on the sorted positional gradients $\{g'_{i,k} | i = 1, \dots, N\}$ [S1].
